---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import History from '../../../Images/History.png';
import ProjectHero from '../../../components/ProjectHero.astro';
import ProjectSection from '../../../components/ProjectSection.astro';
---

<Layout title="Historical Globe Mobile | Batiste COMET-BARTHE" backHref="/en/#projects" lang="en">
  <ProjectHero
    category="Personal project · Android application · World history"
    title="Historical Globe"
    accent="Mobile"
    description="Explore world history through places and eras, then dive deeper with lessons and revision tools."
    tags={['Kotlin', 'Jetpack Compose', 'MapLibre', 'Room / SQLite', 'GeoJSON']}
    image={History}
    imageAlt="Visual identity for the History app, featuring a globe and the app title"
    imageFit="contain"
    technologyLabel="Technologies"
  />

  <section class="px-6 pb-32" style="background: #09090b;">
    <ProjectSection variant="wide">
      <div class="history-project-content">
        <article class="history-project-row">
          <h2>01 — A world-spanning history</h2>
          <div class="history-project-row__body">
            <p>
              History is an educational Android app focused on world history. Its content brings civilizations and events from regions around the world into conversation, moving beyond a narrative centered solely on Europe.
            </p>
            <p>
              The app offers three ways to learn: place events in time, explore them on an interactive globe, and consolidate knowledge with lessons, quizzes, and revision cards.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="history-project-row">
          <h2>02 — Explore the globe</h2>
          <div class="history-project-row__body">
            <p>
              The 3D globe lets users select a country and access its historical context and timeline. GeoJSON data provides a geographic representation of countries; studies associated with specific periods can enrich a selection with a historical name, local context, and rulers.
            </p>
            <p>
              Navigation connects geographic exploration to periods and events: a country is never isolated from its era, and its timeline can be explored from the place concerned.
            </p>
            <div class="history-project-tech">
              <span>MapLibre globe</span>
              <span>Countries &amp; ISO codes</span>
              <span>GeoJSON</span>
              <span>Timelines</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="history-project-row">
          <h2>03 — Learn &amp; revise</h2>
          <div class="history-project-row__body">
            <p>
              Periods provide access to modules organized by theme and region. Each lesson is divided into reading steps, with content written in Markdown and questions to check understanding.
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>Interactive lessons with step-by-step progress and explanatory feedback after each answer.</li>
              <li>Multiple-choice, true-or-false, and fill-in-the-blank questions.</li>
              <li>Anki-inspired revision cards for reviewing events and their dates.</li>
              <li>Country timelines for exploring events in context.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="history-project-row">
          <h2>04 — Architecture &amp; data</h2>
          <div class="history-project-row__body">
            <p>
              The app is built with Kotlin and Jetpack Compose and follows a layered MVVM architecture comprising UI, ViewModel, repository, and data layers. Screens observe the reactive states exposed by ViewModels.
            </p>
            <p>
              Room and SQLite store a pre-populated historical database: periods and sub-periods, countries, events, geographic studies, lesson modules, steps, and questions. Kotlin Coroutines and Flow handle loading and updating the data displayed in the interface.
            </p>
            <div class="history-project-tech">
              <span>Kotlin</span>
              <span>Jetpack Compose</span>
              <span>MVVM</span>
              <span>Room / SQLite</span>
              <span>Coroutines &amp; Flow</span>
              <span>MapLibre GL</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <div class="history-project-footer">
          <p>A personal project bringing together map visualization, data modeling, and the design of educational tools.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/b-cb/History" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            View the project on GitHub
            <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </ProjectSection>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .history-project-content {
    width: min(100%, 74rem);
    margin-inline: auto;
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .history-project-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 2.2fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .history-project-row h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .history-project-row__body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .history-project-row__body p,
  .history-project-footer p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .history-project-row__body ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .history-project-row__body li::marker {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .history-project-tech {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem 1.25rem;
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .history-project-footer {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 300;
  }

  .history-project-footer a {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--footer-link-border);
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
    background: var(--footer-link-bg);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    color: var(--footer-link-text);
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    transition: border-color 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
  }

  .history-project-footer a:hover {
    border-color: var(--footer-link-hover-border);
    color: var(--footer-link-hover-text);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .history-project-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.25rem;
    }

    .history-project-footer {
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
